     {
      "id": "6ad09f43e35e19e82573e423",
      "fieldData": {
       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Salon Waiver Form Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a salon waiver form?\", \"a\": \"A salon waiver form is the document a client reads and signs before a service, confirming they understand its risks and have told the salon about allergies and recent treatments. A salon can ask for one before color or nail work and keep the signed copy with the client's record.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create a salon waiver form?\", \"a\": \"Decide which services need it and what clients agree to, then have a lawyer check the text. Next, describe the form in Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a>. A prompt such as \\\"email the stylist when a color client reports a dye reaction\\\" is enough to start, and Emergent builds the form with an e-signature and the database behind it.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should a hair salon waiver form include?\", \"a\": \"A hair salon waiver form should include the client's name and phone, the service booked, the health questions, the statements the client agrees to, and a signature with the date. Add a line for the stylist's name to show who did the work. Emergent can show those questions one per screen, which reads better on a client's phone than a long page.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should beauty salon waiver forms include for different services?\", \"a\": \"Beauty salon waiver forms should include one shared section every client signs and a short section per service, because a wax and a color appointment raise different concerns. Start the shared section from a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/liability-waiver'>liability waiver form</a>, then add only the questions each service needs.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should a hair salon chemical service waiver form include?\", \"a\": \"A hair salon chemical service waiver form should include questions about past reactions to dye or relaxers, and about any cuts or irritation on the scalp. The FDA's hair dye guidance tells consumers: \\\"Do a patch test on your skin every time before dyeing your hair.\\\" Add fields for the patch test date and its result.\"}, {\"q\": \"When do you use a hair salon client waiver form?\", \"a\": \"Use a hair salon client waiver form before every service it covers, and send it with the booking confirmation, which keeps the front desk from waiting on a signature at check-in. Ask a returning client to sign again whenever a health answer changes, such as a new allergy or medication.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can I make a hair salon waiver form for free?\", \"a\": \"Yes: Emergent is free to start, and the free tier covers building and publishing a hair salon waiver form. If a client only needs to agree to one treatment, such as a lightening service, a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/consent'>consent form</a> may be the simpler document.\"}, {\"q\": \"Where can I find a hair salon waiver form free template?\", \"a\": \"WaiverForever runs a free generator for salon and spa waivers that covers hair, nails, waxing, and other beauty services. The same page recommends having a legal professional review the final waiver for your jurisdiction. Do the same with any free template you start from.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do you set up a salon waiver form as a hair stylist renting a booth?\", \"a\": \"Put your own name and business at the top of the salon waiver form instead of the salon's, and keep one record per client with every waiver they have signed, newest first. Ask the owner whether the salon wants a copy as well.\"}, {\"q\": \"What questions go on a nail salon waiver form?\", \"a\": \"A nail salon waiver form should ask about allergies to acrylic or gel products and about cuts or skin conditions on the hands and feet. Leave space for any other health detail the client wants the technician to know. If you post photos of a client's nail art, ask them to sign a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/model-release'>model release form</a> as well.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
      }
     }
    ]
